From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: Detect output HDR state by default on Win32.

The active-output checks in dxgi-respect-output-hdr-state.patch already
prevent HDR10 from being reported for SDR or unqueryable outputs. Default
the Win32 HDR policy to enabled so these checks can detect HDR without
requiring PROTON_ENABLE_HDR, PROTON_USE_HDR, or DXVK_HDR.

Keep explicit DXVK_HDR and dxgi.enableHDR settings, and let DXVK_NO_HDR=1
disable HDR even when a configuration file enables it. Preserve the UE4
D3D11 compatibility exclusions, the Vulkan surface-format requirement,
and the existing opt-in policy for non-Win32 WSI backends.

Apply after dxgi-respect-output-hdr-state.patch. Wine Wayland already
reports compositor color-management state; the matching Wine fixup adds
Gamescope XWayland feedback and consistent disable handling.

Manual validation after rebuilding:
- Native Wayland HDR output, no HDR flags: game HDR becomes available.
- SDR output and mixed SDR/HDR monitors: only the HDR output reports HDR.
- Gamescope HDR on/off and ordinary XWayland SDR.
- DXVK_HDR=0, DXVK_NO_HDR=1, and dxgi.enableHDR=False.
- DX11, DX12 (which shares DXGI), and native Vulkan games using NVAPI.
---

diff --git a/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.cpp b/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.cpp
--- a/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.cpp
+++ b/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.cpp
@@ -199,7 +199,14 @@
       this->hideIntelGpu = true;
     }
 
-    this->enableHDR = config.getOption<bool>("dxgi.enableHDR", env::getEnvVar("DXVK_HDR") == "1");
+    const std::string hdr = env::getEnvVar("DXVK_HDR");
+    bool enableHdrDefault = hdr == "1";
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    // Wine reports the active output state; HDR10 also needs surface support.
+    enableHdrDefault |= hdr.empty();
+#endif
+    this->enableHDR = config.getOption<bool>("dxgi.enableHDR", enableHdrDefault)
+                  && env::getEnvVar("DXVK_NO_HDR") != "1";
 
     bool enableUe4Workarounds = config.getOption<bool>("dxgi.enableUe4Workarounds", false);

